'''Dimitri Leslie Roger''' (born July 13, 1992),<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.ascap.com/repertory#ace/search/workID/898046413 |title=ACE Title Search |access-date=November 17, 2020 |archive-date=June 12, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160612055619/https://www.ascap.com/Home/ace-title-search/index.aspx#ace/search/workID/898046413 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/07/happy-birthday-rich-the-kid/|title=HAPPY BIRTHDAY, RICH THE KID!|work=XXL|author=Madden, Sidney|date=July 13, 2017|access-date=March 3, 2020}}</ref> known professionally as '''Rich the Kid''', is an American rapper. After a number of independent mixtapes, he signed with [[Interscope Records]] in 2017 to release his debut studio album, ''[[The World Is Yours (Rich the Kid album)|The World Is Yours]]'' (2018). Supported by his best known singles "[[New Freezer]]" (featuring [[Kendrick Lamar]]) and "[[Plug Walk]]", the album peaked at number two on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]]. His second and third studio albums, ''[[The World Is Yours 2]]'' (2019) and ''[[Boss Man (album)|Boss Man]]'' (2020) peaked at numbers four and 24 on the chart, respectively. He has also released the collaborative mixtapes ''[[Nobody Safe]]'' (2020) with [[YoungBoy Never Broke Again]], and ''[[Trust Fund Babies]]'' (2021) with [[Lil Wayne]]. Furthermore, he founded the record label [[#Rich Forever Music|Rich Forever Music]] in 2016, through which he has signed rappers [[Famous Dex]] and [[Jay Critch]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://thesource.com/2023/04/14/famous-dex-is-nearly-a-year-sober-and-returning-to-music-with-rich-forever-5/|title=Famous Dex is Nearly a Year Sober and Returning to Rich Forever Music|website=TheSource.com|date=April 14, 2023 }}</ref>

His 2024 single, "[[Carnival (¥$ song)|Carnival]]" (with [[¥$]] featuring [[Playboi Carti]]) marked a period of resurgence as it peaked atop the ''Billboard'' Hot 100, becoming his first song to do so. Its co-performers, [[Kanye West]] and [[Ty Dolla Sign]], both served as executive producers for Roger's fourth studio album, ''[[Life's a Gamble (Rich the Kid album)|Life's a Gamble]]'' (2024), which failed to chart in any known territory.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/rich-the-kid-kanye-west-offset-new-album-lifes-a-gamble|title=Rich The Kid Taps Kanye West, Offset & More For New Album 'Life's A Gamble'|website=HiphopDX.com|date=January 30, 2024}}</ref>

==Early life==
Dimitri Leslie Roger was born in [[Queens]], New York City, on July 13, 1992.<ref name="wmag">{{cite web | url=http://www.wmagazine.com/story/new-york-fashion-week-mens-rich-the-kid | title=Following Rapper Rich the Kid Around Men's Fashion Week | work=[[W (magazine)|W Magazine]] | date=July 15, 2016 | access-date=August 16, 2016 |author=Petrarca, Emilia}}</ref> He is of [[Haitian Americans|Haitian]] descent and grew up speaking [[Haitian Creole]] fluently.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/6443843/univeral-label-rap-hit-squad | title=The Lowdown on Atlanta Hip-Hop Label Quality Control's Young Hot Squad -- From Migos to OG Maco | magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] | date=January 21, 2015 | access-date=August 17, 2016 | author=Peisner, David}}</ref><ref name="xxlmag">{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/the-break/2013/12/the-break-presents-rich-the-kid/|last=Diep|first=Eric|title=The Break Presents: Rich The Kid|work=[[XXL (magazine)|XXL Magazine]]|date=December 2, 2013|access-date=November 3, 2014}}</ref> After his parents' divorce, Roger moved with his mother to [[College Park, Georgia]], when he was 13.<ref name="xxlmag" /><ref>{{cite magazine | url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/rich-the-kid-from-the-streets-exclusive-video-premiere-6415110/ | title=Rich the Kid, 'From the Streets': Exclusive Video Premiere | magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] | date=December 23, 2014 | access-date=August 17, 2016 | author=Ramirez, Erika}}</ref>

Rich the Kid grew up listening to [[Nas]], [[Jay-Z]], [[Tupac Shakur|2Pac]], [[the Notorious B.I.G.]], and [[50 Cent]], but after moving to College Park, he began listening to [[Southern hip hop]] artists including [[T.I.]] and [[Jeezy]].<ref name="xxlmag" /> His first rap name was Black Boy Da Kid,<ref name="wmag" /> but later changed it to Rich the Kid. He attended [[Elmont Memorial Junior – Senior High School]] in [[Elmont, New York]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/richthekid/status/44850robynlithe9371052724224|title=@HandsomeBobby5 yea went to elmont & Alden Terrace|last=KID|first=RICH THE|date=March 25, 2014|website=@richthekid|access-date=March 2, 2018}}</ref>

==Career==
===2013–2016: Career beginnings, Rich Forever, and early mixtapes===
[[File:Rich The Kid.png|thumb|left|155px|Rich the Kid in May 2016]]
In 2013, he released his debut solo [[mixtape]], ''Been About the Benjamins'',<ref name="hotnewhiphop">{{cite web | url=http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid/profile/ | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151123203731/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid/profile/ | url-status=dead | archive-date=November 23, 2015 | title=Rich The Kid | work=HotNewHipHop| access-date=August 16, 2016}}</ref> and later that year released a collaborative mixtape series with [[Migos]] called ''Streets On Lock'' (volume 1 and 2), with volume 3 being released in 2014 and volume 4 being released in 2015.<ref name="hotnewhiphop" /> His second solo mixtape titled ''Feels Good 2 Be Rich'' was released in August 2014, and featured artists Migos, [[Young Thug]], [[Kirko Bangz]], [[Rockie Fresh]], [[Stalley]], [[Soulja Boy]], [[Riff Raff (rapper)|RiFF RaFF]], [[Jeremih]], [[K Camp]], [[Young Dolph]], [[Yo Gotti]], [[French Montana]], [[Chinx]] & [[Kodak Black]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-feels-good-to-be-rich-new-mixtape.115442.html | title=Rich The Kid – Feels Good To Be Rich [New Mixtape] | work=HotNewHipHop | date=August 14, 2014 | access-date=August 17, 2016 |last=Rose |first=Lilah | archive-date=July 14, 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160714081927/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-feels-good-to-be-rich-new-mixtape.115442.html | url-status=dead }}</ref> In November 2014, Rich the Kid released the single "On My Way" featuring GS9 artists, [[Bobby Shmurda]] & [[Rowdy Rebel]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/564372-rich-the-kid-on-my-way-feat-bobby-shmurda-rowdy-rebel-prod-by-zaytoven-new-song|title=Rich The Kid – On My Way Feat. Bobby Shmurda & Rowdy Rebel|last=Lyons|first=Patrick|date=November 4, 2014|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=February 21, 2015}}</ref> In December 2014, he released his third mixtape ''[[Rich Than Famous]]'' which featured [[YG (rapper)|YG]], Migos, Bobby Shmurda, Rowdy Rebel, [[Gucci Mane]], Johnny Cinco and [[Peewee Longway|PeeWee Longway]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-rich-than-famous-new-mixtape.115629.html|title=Rich Than Famous|work=HotNewHipHop|last=Rose|first=Lilah|access-date=September 26, 2018|archive-date=February 7, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220207134841/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-rich-than-famous-new-mixtape.115629.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Rich the Kid's first release in 2015 was a collaborative mixtape titled ''Still On Lock'' with Migos.<ref name="spinrilla">{{cite web|url=https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/migos-rich-the-kid-still-on-lock|title=Still On Lock by Migos & Rich The Kid|date=May 19, 2015|publisher=Spinrilla|access-date=July 20, 2016|archive-date=August 17, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160817190217/https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/migos-rich-the-kid-still-on-lock|url-status=dead}}</ref> In August 2015, he released ''[[Flexxin on Purpose|Flexin' on Purpose]]''. The 14-track project featured collaborations with [[Master P]], [[Young Dolph]], [[Ty Dolla Sign|Ty Dolla $ign]], [[Fetty Wap]] and [[Rich Homie Quan]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://hiphopdx.com/news/id.35986/title.migos-x-rich-the-kid-streets-on-lock-4-release-date-cover-art-tracklist-download-mixtape-stream | title=Migos x Rich The Kid "Streets On Lock 4" Release Date, Cover Art, Tracklist, Download & Mixtape Stream |last=Hernandez |first=Victoria | work=[[HipHopDX]] | date=October 22, 2015 | access-date=August 17, 2016}}</ref> In October 2015, he released Streets On Lock 4 with Migos with features from Jose Guapo, Skippa Da Flippa, Hoodrich Pablo Juan, Lil Duke, [[2 Chainz]], [[Jeezy]], [[Waka Flocka Flame|Waka Flocka]], Young Dolph, PeeWee Longway, Mango Foo, [[Slim Jxmmi]], [[iLoveMakonnen]], Tray1, Migo Domingo, Migo Jerz, YRN Lingo and [[Young Greatness]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/32807-migos-and-rich-the-kid-streets-on-lock-4-new-mixtape|title=Streets On Lock 4|last=Goddard|first=Kevin|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=September 26, 2018|archive-date=April 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230411234319/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/32807-migos-and-rich-the-kid-streets-on-lock-4-new-mixtape|url-status=live}}</ref>

Rich the Kid and iLoveMakonnen released ''Whip It'', featuring 8 tracks on Thanksgiving Day, November 26, 2015, with guest spots from [[Rome Fortune]], Migos, [[T-Wayne]] and Key!.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vibe.com/2015/11/rich-the-kid-ilovemakonnens-whip-it-mixtape/ | title=Stream Rich The Kid & ILoveMakonnen's 'Whip It Mixtape' | work=[[Vibe (magazine)|Vibe Magazine]] |last=Fresh |first=Mikey | date=November 26, 2015 | access-date=August 17, 2016 | archive-date=September 20, 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160920111526/http://www.vibe.com/2015/11/rich-the-kid-ilovemakonnens-whip-it-mixtape/ | url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine | url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/watch-steve-aoki-rich-the-kid-ilovemakonnen-host-rager-in-how-else-video-20160629 | title=Watch Steve Aoki, Rich the Kid, ILoveMakonnen Host Rager in 'How Else' Video | magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] | date=June 29, 2016 | access-date=August 16, 2016 | last=Spanos | first=Brittany | archive-date=August 26, 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160826131852/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/watch-steve-aoki-rich-the-kid-ilovemakonnen-host-rager-in-how-else-video-20160629 | url-status=dead }}</ref> The next month ''[[Dabbin Fever]]'' was released on Christmas Eve 2015, with features from [[Wiz Khalifa]], Migos, Skippa Da Flippa, [[21 Savage]], ManMan Savage, Jose Guapo, [[Playboi Carti]], Kodak Black and [[Currensy|Curren$y]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://hiphopdx.com/news/id.36783/title.rich-the-kid-dabbin-fever-mixtape-stream-cover-art-tracklist-download|title=Rich The Kid "Dabbin Fever" Mixtape Stream, Cover Art, Tracklist & Download|work=[[HipHopDX]]|date=December 25, 2015|access-date=August 17, 2016|last=Hernandez|first=Victoria}}</ref> He released his ''[[Trap Talk]]'' mixtape in April 2016, which features 21 Savage, Ty Dolla $ign, Playboi Carti, Kodak Black, Migos, [[Famous Dex]] and [[PartyNextDoor]].<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/stream-rich-the-kid-trap-talk-mixtape-premiere-7340633/|title=Stream Rich The Kid's New 'Trap Talk' Mixtape: Premiere|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard Magazine]]|date=April 19, 2016|access-date=August 16, 2016|last=Rys|first=Dan}}</ref>

In March 2016, Rich founded his record label, Rich Forever Music.<ref name="RFM1"/><ref name="RFM2"/> In October 2016, he released his mixtape ''[[Keep Flexin]]'' which featured [[Desiigner]], Migos, Famous Dex, Jeremih, Young Thug and Playboi Carti.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/47298-rich-the-kid-keep-flexin-new-mixtape|title=Keep Flexin|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref>

===2017–2018: Rise to fame, commercial success and ''The World Is Yours''===
In May 2017, he collaborated as a featured artist on the [[Diplo]] song, "[[Bankroll (song)|Bankroll]]", which also features [[Rich Brian]] and [[Young Thug]] (the song originally featured [[Justin Bieber]] instead of Rich Brian).<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/hear-justin-bieber-rap-on-diplos-rubbery-new-song-bankroll-w481974|title=Hear Justin Bieber Rap on Diplo's Rubbery New Song 'Bankroll'|last=Spanos|first=Brittany|date=May 11, 2017|magazine=Rolling Stone|access-date=May 12, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thefader.com/2017/05/11/justin-bieber-diplo-bankroll-rich-the-kid-young-thug|title=Listen To Justin Bieber Rap On Diplo's 'Bankroll' With Rich The Kid And Young Thug|last=Darville|first=Jordan|date=May 11, 2017|website=The FADER|access-date=May 12, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Citation|title=Diplo – Bank Roll Feat. Justin Bieber, Young Thug & Rich The Kid {{!}} Stream [New Song]|work=HotNewHipHop |date=May 11, 2017|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/594095-diplo-bank-roll-feat-justin-bieber-young-thug-and-rich-the-kid-new-song|access-date=May 12, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/dance/7792851/justin-bieber-bankroll-diplo-young-thug-rich-kid|title=Listen to Justin Bieber Rap on Diplo's 'Bankroll' Collab With Young Thug & Rich the Kid|last=Bein|first=Kat|date=May 11, 2017|magazine=Billboard|access-date=May 12, 2017}}</ref>

On June 9, 2017, Rich the Kid announced that he had signed to [[Interscope Records]].<ref name="Xxlmag.com">{{cite web |date=June 9, 2017 |title=Rich The Kid Signs to Interscope Records – XXL |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/06/rich-the-kid-signs-interscope/ |access-date=June 10, 2017 |publisher=Xxlmag.com}}</ref> In an interview with ''[[XXL (magazine)|XXL]]'', Roger talked about his decision on signing with Interscope:<ref name="Xxlmag.com" />
<blockquote>I was talking to different labels, [[Columbia Records|Columbia]], [[RCA Records|RCA]], [[Epic Records|Epic]], I decided not to sign with Epic even after [[L.A. Reid]] offered me a crazy deal. [Senior Vice President of A&R at Interscope] Manny Smith & Interscope CEO [[John Janick]] understand me and my vision for myself and also my label. Interscope gave me the opportunity to take over the game completely and that's what I'm going to do.</blockquote>

Rich the Kid released the single "[[New Freezer]]" featuring [[Kendrick Lamar]] on September 26, 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/64905-kendrick-lamar-joins-rich-the-kid-on-new-freezer-new-song|title=Kendrick Lamar Joins Rich The Kid On 'New Freezer'|website=HNHH|last=Smith|first=Trevor|date=September 26, 2017|access-date=June 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170926223401/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kendrick-lamar-joins-rich-the-kid-on-new-freezer-new-song.1975786.html|archive-date=September 26, 2017 |url-status=live}}</ref> The track marked Rich's first appearance on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], peaking at number 41 on the charts.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/rich-the-kid-new-freezer-kendrick-lamar-hot-100-debut/|title=Rich The Kid Makes Billboard Hot 100 Debut With Kendrick Lamar Collaboration 'New Freezer'|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Zellner|first=Xander|date=February 6, 2017|access-date=February 13, 2024|archive-date=June 10, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230610022957/https://www.billboard.com/pro/rich-the-kid-new-freezer-kendrick-lamar-hot-100-debut/|url-status=live}}</ref> On February 9, 2018, Rich the Kid released "[[Plug Walk]]".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.complex.com/music/2018/02/rich-the-kid-premieres-plug-walk-reveals-features-on-debut-album|title=Rich the Kid Premieres "Plug Walk" and Reveals Features on Debut Album|publisher=[[Complex (magazine)|Complex]]|date=February 8, 2018|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The track proceeded to become Rich's highest-charting single at the time on the Hot 100 after peaking at number 13 and received a remix featuring Gucci Mane, YG, and 2 Chainz, released on June 20, 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2018/06/rich-the-kid-plug-walk-remix-gucci-mane-yg-2-chainz/|title=Rich The Kid Taps Gucci Mane, YG, 2 Chainz on "Plug Walk (Remix)"|last=Burks|first=Tosten|website=XXL Mag|date=June 20, 2018 |access-date=June 27, 2018}}</ref> "Dead Friends" was released on March 26, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.complex.com/music/2018/03/rich-the-kid-drops-lil-uzi-vert-diss-dead-friends|title=Rich the Kid Drops Full Version of Lil Uzi Vert Diss "Dead Friends"|work=Complex|last=Cowen|first=Trace William|date=March 26, 2018|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The three singles apeered on Rich's debut studio album, ''[[The World Is Yours (Rich the Kid album)|The World Is Yours]]'' with guest appearances from [[Lil Wayne]], [[Swae Lee]], [[Quavo]], [[Offset (rapper)|Offset]], [[Trippie Redd]], [[Khalid (American singer)|Khalid]], [[Kendrick Lamar]], [[Rick Ross]], [[Future (rapper)|Future]], [[Jay Critch]] and [[Chris Brown]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/02/rich-the-kid-chris-brown-lil-wayne-more-upcoming-album/|title=Rich The Kid Confirms Chris Brown and More on Upcoming Album – XXL|website=XXL Mag|date=February 9, 2018 |access-date=June 17, 2018}}</ref> It debuted at number two on the US [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]], marking his second US top 10 album.<ref name="BB200">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/the-weeknd-no-1-album-billboard-200-my-dear-melancholy/|title=The Weeknd Scores Third Consecutive No. 1 Album on Billboard 200 Chart With 'My Dear Melancholy'|magazine=Billboard|first=Keith|last=Caulfield|date=April 8, 2018|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> In 2018, he also opened for Chris Brown's "[[Heartbreak on a Full Moon Tour]]".<ref>{{Cite web | title=Chris Brown Announces 'Heartbreak on a Full Moon' Tour Lineup | url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/chris-brown-heartbreak-on-a-full-moon-tour-dates-8262810/ | access-date=2026-09-14 | website=www.billboard.com}}</ref>

===2019-2021: ''The World Is Yours 2'', ''Boss Man'', and collaborative mixtapes===
On January 9, 2019, Rich released the official music video for the December 2018-released, "[[Splashin]]".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/127793-rich-the-kid-comes-through-splashin-on-his-new-single-new-song|title=Rich The Kid Comes Through "Splashin" On His New Single|work=HotNewHipHop|last=A.|first=Aron|date=December 3, 2018|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/138307-rich-the-kid-channels-a-tna-loving-mad-scientist-in-splashin-new-video|title=Rich The Kid Channels A "TNA" Loving Mad Scientist In "Splashin"|work=HotNewHipHop|last=Findlay|first=Mitch|date=January 9, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> Months later, on March 1, 2019, Rich released the single, "4 Phones" while also announcing his sophomore full-length studio album and the sequel to his debut, ''[[The World Is Yours 2]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2019/02/rich-the-kid-announces-the-world-is-yours-2-release-date-4-phones|title=Rich the Kid Announces Release Date for 'The World Is Yours 2'|work=[[Complex (magazine)|Complex]]|last=Ortiz|first=Edwin|date=February 28, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://hiphop-n-more.com/2019/03/rich-the-kid-4-phones-new-song/|title=Rich The Kid Announces 'The World is Yours 2' Release Date; Unveils New Single '4 Phones'|work=HipHop-N-More|author=Navjosh|date=March 1, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://rapradar.com/2019/03/01/new-video-rich-the-kid-4-phones/|title=New Video: Rich The Kid "4 Phones"|work=Rap Rader|author=Big Homie|date=March 1, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The album's third single, "Tic Toc" with [[Tory Lanez]] was released on March 14, 2019,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/156223-rich-the-kid-preps-the-world-is-yours-2-with-tory-lanez-featured-tic-toc-new-song|title=Rich The Kid Preps "The World Is Yours 2" With Tory Lanez Featured "Tic Toc"|work=HotNewHipHop|last=Zidel|first=Alex|date=March 14, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> just a week prior to the release of the album. ''The World Is Yours 2'' released with features from [[Big Sean]], [[YoungBoy Never Broke Again]], [[Lil Pump]], [[Takeoff (rapper)|Takeoff]], [[Offset (rapper)|Offset]], [[Tory Lanez]], [[Young Thug]], [[Gunna (rapper)|Gunna]], [[Miguel (singer)|Miguel]], [[A Boogie wit da Hoodie]], [[Jay Critch]], [[Nav (rapper)|Nav]], and [[Ty Dolla Sign]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/181554-rich-the-kids-the-world-is-yours-2-is-packed-big-sean-nba-youngboy-lil-pump-and-more-news|title=Rich The Kid's "The World Is Yours 2" Has Big Sean, NBA YoungBoy, Lil Pump, & More|work=HotNewHipHop|last=Zidel|first=Alex|date=March 12, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The album proceeded to debut at number 4 on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]] US albums chart.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/nav-nets-first-no-1-album-on-billboard-200-chart-with-bad-habits/|title=NAV Nets First No. 1 Album on Billboard 200 Chart With 'Bad Habits'|magazine=Billboard|last=Caulfield|first=Keith|date=March 31, 2019|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref>

On December 6, 2019, it was announced that Rich the Kid departed [[Interscope Records]] and signed with [[Republic Records]], while still remaining under the [[UMG]] umbrella while releasing the lead single to his next album, "That's Tuff" featuring Quavo.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2019/12/rich-the-kid-quavo-thats-tuff|title=Rich the Kid Leaves Interscope for Republic Records, Shares "That's Tuff" f/ Quavo|work=[[Complex (magazine)|Complex]]|last1=C. Mahadevan|first1=Tara|last2=Diep|first2=Eric|date=December 6, 2019|access-date=April 5, 2020}}</ref> The album's second single, "Money Talk" featuring YoungBoy Never Broke Again was released on January 17, 2020.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/231555-rich-the-kid-and-nba-youngboy-bond-over-their-love-for-guap-in-money-talk-video-new-video|title=Rich The Kid & NBA Youngboy Bond Over Their Love Of Guap In "Money Talk" Video|work=[[HotNewHipHop]]|last=C.|first=Noah|date=January 21, 2020|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The final two singles, "Red" was released on March 6, 2020, just a week prior to the album's release.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://consequence.net/2020/03/rich-the-kid-new-album-bossman-red-stream/|title=Rich the Kid Announces New Album Bossman, Shares "Red": Stream|website=[[Consequence of Sound]]|last=Graves|first=Wren|date=March 7, 2020|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> On March 13, 2020, Rich released his third full-length studio album, ''[[Boss Man (album)|Boss Man]]'', featuring guest appearances from [[Lil Baby]], [[DaBaby]], [[Nicki Minaj]], [[Post Malone]], [[Lil Tjay]], [[YoungBoy Never Broke Again]], [[London on da Track]], and [[Quavo]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rap-up.com/2020/03/12/rich-the-kid-boss-man-tracklist/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200317063013/https://www.rap-up.com/2020/03/12/rich-the-kid-boss-man-tracklist/|url-status=dead|archive-date=March 17, 2020|title=Rich the Kid Reveals 'Boss Man' Tracklist|work=[[Rap-Up]]|date=March 12, 2020|access-date=April 5, 2020}}</ref>

In February 2020, it was announced that Rich would leave Republic and sign a distribution deal with [[Empire Distribution]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.60390/title.rich-the-kid-reflects-on-dropping-nearly-1m-to-exit-1st-record-deal-as-his-independent-rap-empire-grows#signup|title = Rich the Kid Reflects on Dropping Nearly $1M to Exit 1st Record Deal as His Independent Rap Empire Grows|date = February 3, 2020}}</ref> On October 16, 2020, Rich teamed up with NBA YoungBoy for the single, "Bankroll".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/289858-rich-the-kid-and-nba-youngboy-brag-about-their-bankroll-new-song|title=Rich The Kid & NBA Youngboy Brag About Their "Bankroll"|work=HotNewHipHop|last=Marie|first=Erika|date=October 16, 2020|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> On November 13, the duo released "Automatic",<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.revolt.tv/article/2020-11-13/65907/rich-the-kid-and-youngboy-never-broke-again-drop-new-song-automatic/|title=Rich the Kid and YoungBoy Never Broke Again drop new song "Automatic"|work=[[Revolt (TV network)|Revolt TV]]|last=Cho|first=Regina|date=November 13, 2020|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> just a week later, on November 20, the duo's collaborative mixtape, [[Nobody Safe]] was released.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/a/j-rose/rich-the-kid-youngboy-never-broke-again-nobody-safe-album-stream|title=Rich the Kid and YoungBoy Never Broke Again Connect for Joint Album 'Nobody Safe'|work=[[Complex Networks|Complex]]|last=Rose|first=Jordan|date=November 20, 2020|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref>

On April 14, 2021, Rich the Kid signed a multi-million dollar deal with [[Rostrum Records]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=April 14, 2021|title=Rich The Kid Signs Multi-Million Dollar Deal With Mac Miller & Wiz Khalifa's Former Label|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.61580/title.rich-the-kid-signs-multi-million-dollar-deal-with-mac-miller-wiz-khalifas-former-label|access-date=April 16, 2021|website=HipHopDX}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|title=Rich The Kid Signs With Rostrum Records|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/business/9556192/rich-the-kid-rostrum-records/|access-date=April 16, 2021|magazine=Billboard}}</ref> This was followed by the release of "[[Feelin' Like Tunechi]]" with [[Lil Wayne]] on October 1, 2021.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Powell |first1=Jon |title=Lil Wayne and Rich The Kid are "Feeling Like Tunechi" in new video |url=https://www.revolt.tv/article/2021-10-01/107626/lil-wayne-and-rich-the-kid-are-feeling-like-tunechi-in-new-video/ |website=[[Revolt (TV network)|Revolt]] |date=October 1, 2021|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Robinson |first1=Joshua |title=Lil Wayne Recreates His Iconic 2012 Deposition In The "Feelin' Like Tunechi" Video |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/357751-lil-wayne-recreates-his-iconic-2012-deposition-in-the-feelin-like-tunechi-video-new-song |website=[[HotNewHipHop]] |date=October 1, 2021|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The song was then followed by the release of the duo's collaborative mixtape, ''[[Trust Fund Babies]]'' that same day.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rap-up.com/2021/09/30/lil-wayne-rich-the-kid-trust-fund-babies-stream/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211001040734/https://www.rap-up.com/2021/09/30/lil-wayne-rich-the-kid-trust-fund-babies-stream/|url-status=dead|archive-date=October 1, 2021|title=Lil Wayne and Rich the Kid Drop Joint Mixtape 'Trust Fund Babies|work=[[Rap-Up]]|date=October 9, 2021|access-date=September 30, 2021}}</ref>

===2022–present: Return of Rich Forever and ''Life's A Gamble''===
On November 14, 2022, Rich the Kid signed with [[RCA Records]] and released the single, "Motion".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Panaligan |first=E. J. |date=2022-11-14 |title=Rich the Kid Signs with RCA Records, Releases New Single 'Motion' (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2022/music/news/rich-the-kid-signs-with-rca-records-1235427246/ |access-date=2022-11-15 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>
[[File:Rich The Kid Bologna.jpg|thumb|Rich The Kid, standing on the top of his car, right after ¥$’ listening party for their album ''[[Vultures 1]]'', in [[Bologna, Italy]] (2024)]]
In mid-2023, he began work on ''Rich Forever 5'', announcing that he, [[Famous Dex]], and [[Jay Critch]] have reunited.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Dolman |first1=Madison |title=Rich The Kid Exclusive Interview: Takeoff Memories, Advice to Young Artists & New Album Rich Forever 5 |url=https://sidedoormag.com/blog/2023/4/10/exclusive-interview-with-rich-the-kid-interview-talks-takeoff-memories-creative-process-release-dates-for-rich-forever-5-more/ |website=Sidedoor Magazine |date=April 10, 2023|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> This was followed by the release of his collaborative single with both rappers, "Big Dawg" in December 2023.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Horvath |first1=Zachary |title=Rich The Kid, Jay Critch, And Famous Dex Reunite On "Big Dawg" |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/745154-rich-the-kid-famous-dex-jay-critch-big-dawg |website=[[HotNewHipHop]] |date=December 15, 2023|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> The trio then released "Rich & Reckless" in January 2024, while Rich announced the title for his fourth studio album to be ''Life's A Gamble''.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mendez |first1=Marisa |title=RICH THE KID TAPS KANYE WEST, OFFSET & MORE FOR NEW ALBUM 'LIFE'S A GAMBLE' |url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/rich-the-kid-kanye-west-offset-new-album-lifes-a-gamble |website=[[HipHopDX]] |date=January 30, 2024|access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref> On February 10, 2024, Rich the Kid guest performed alongside [[Playboi Carti]] on the single "[[Carnival (¥$ song)|Carnival]]" by [[Kanye West]] and [[Ty Dolla Sign]], from their collaborative album ''[[Vultures 1]]''. It peaked atop the ''Billboard'' Hot 100, becoming his first song to do so. Capitalizing on its success, on June 22 of that year, he released "Gimme a Second 2", a collaborative single with West featuring Ty Dolla Sign and [[Peso Pluma]]. It was released by the record label [[gamma.]] and is serving as the lead single for his forthcoming album, ''[[Life's a Gamble (Rich the Kid album)|Life's a Gamble]]'', which is slated for release in July.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://hypebeast.com/2024/6/rich-the-kid-ye-ty-dolla-sign-gimme-a-second-2-single-stream | title=Rich the Kid Taps Ye, Ty Dolla $ign for "Gimme a Second 2" | date=June 22, 2024 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Lamarre |first=Carl |date=February 10, 2024 |title=Kanye West & Ty Dolla $ign Team Up for New Album 'Vultures 1': Stream It Now |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-ty-dolla-sign-vultures-1-album-stream-it-now-1235558698/ |access-date=February 11, 2024 |magazine=Billboard |language=en-US |archive-date=February 10, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240210213649/https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-ty-dolla-sign-vultures-1-album-stream-it-now-1235558698/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2026, he starred in the action film ''Conspiracy of Thieves'', directed by [[Randall Emmett]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2026/02/randall-emmett-movie-emile-hirsch-busta-rhymes-rich-the-kid-1236714853/|title=Voltage Launches Randall Emmett-Directed 'Conspiracy Of Thieves' With Emile Hirsch, Busta Rhymes, Dash Mihok, Rich The Kid - EFM|website=Deadline|first=Andreas|last=Wiseman|date=February 10, 2026|access-date=August 3, 2026}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Roger was married to Antonette Willis and has two children with her. In March 2018, Willis filed for divorce, seeking full physical custody while giving Roger visitation rights and joint legal custody. Willis is also seeking spousal support.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/03/rich-the-kid-wife-files-for-divorce/|title=Rich The Kid's Wife Files for Divorce – XXL|website=XXL Mag|date=March 22, 2018 |access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> This was shortly after Willis accused him of cheating on her with [[Blac Chyna]] and India Love, even alleging that he was in a relationship with the former.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/03/rich-the-kid-accused-of-cheating-on-wife-with-blac-chyna-india-love/|title=Rich The Kid Accused of Cheating With Blac Chyna, India Love|website=XXL Mag|date=March 20, 2018 |access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> Willis later claimed that Roger abused her and forced her to have abortions regularly, saying it was commonplace for police to be called to their residence for domestic abuse.<ref name=":0">{{Cite news|url=https://www.spin.com/2018/05/rich-the-kid-domestic-abuse-forced-abortions/|title=Rich the Kid Accused of Domestic Abuse, Forcing Ex to Get Abortions: Report|date=May 22, 2018|work=Spin|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2016/10/rich-the-kid-accused-domestic-violence/|title=Rich The Kid Accused of Domestic Violence – XXL|website=XXL Mag|date=October 3, 2016 |access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref>

Roger began dating Tori Hughes (professionally known as Tori Brixx) shortly following the filing of the divorce. On June 15, 2018, Roger was hospitalized following a home invasion at Hughes' home.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/rich-the-kid-hospitalized-home-invasion-8461272/|title=Rich the Kid Hospitalized Following Home Invasion: Report|magazine=Billboard|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> According to a police report, several men entered Hughes' home carrying firearms and demanded money. When Roger attempted to confront them, he was beaten by them and the men left with a "significant" amount of money and jewelry.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/rich-the-kid-hospitalized-after-home-invasion-attack-report/|title=Rich the Kid Hospitalized After Home Invasion Attack: Report {{!}} Pitchfork|website=pitchfork.com|date=June 15, 2018|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> On December 29, 2018, Rich the Kid got into a UTV accident in Calabasas, CA, when Dimitri and his friend were driving around in a Polaris RZR 4-wheeler. Based on sources from TMZ, it seems that Dimitri lost control of it and fell off of his RZR 4-wheeler and severely injured his hand. He was taken to the hospital shortly after.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.tmz.com/2018/12/29/rich-the-kid-injures-hand-utv-accident-crash/|title=Rich the Kid Severely Injures His Hand in UTV Crash|website=Tmz.com|date=December 29, 2018 |access-date=June 7, 2023}}</ref> In February 2019, he was robbed and shot at outside of the [[Westlake Recording Studios|Westlake Recording Studio]] in [[West Hollywood, California|West Hollywood]], California.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://people.com/music/rich-the-kid-shot-at-robbed-recording-studio-usher-inside/|title=Rapper Rich the Kid Shot at and Robbed Outside a West Hollywood Studio as Usher Records Inside|website=PEOPLE.com|access-date=February 19, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.ajc.com/entertainment/rapper-rich-the-kid-robbed-outside-studio-where-usher-was-recording/fcH3gup4qBq4bXB52flnJM/|title=Rapper Rich the Kid robbed outside studio where Usher was recording|last=Nancy Clanton|first=The Atlanta Journal-Constitution|newspaper=The Atlanta Journal-Constitution|access-date=February 19, 2019}}</ref>

==Feuds==
===Lil Uzi Vert===
Rich the Kid and [[Lil Uzi Vert]]'s feud started on Twitter following a highly publicized label issue Lil Uzi Vert had with [[DJ Drama]]'s Generation Now imprint in January 2018.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/rich-the-kid-lil-uzi-vert-feud-timeline-8221703/|title=A Timeline of Rich The Kid's Feud With Lil Uzi Vert|magazine=Billboard|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> Rich the Kid tweeted at Lil Uzi Vert, offering them a position in his imprint Rich Forever Music, in which Uzi replied "Boy I'm not signing for 20 racks".<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.highsnobiety.com/p/rich-the-kid-lil-uzi-vert-diss-track/|title=Rich the Kid Previews a Lil Uzi Vert Diss Track|date=June 16, 2018|work=Highsnobiety|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://twitter.com/liluzivert/status/951950177233002497?lang=en|title=Uzi London 🌎☄️💕® on Twitter|work=Twitter|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/02/rich-the-kid-lil-uzi-vert-diss/|title=Rich The Kid Previews Lil Uzi Vert Diss Track – XXL|website=XXL Mag|date=February 28, 2018 |access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> A month later on February 9, 2018, Rich The Kid said that he and Lil Uzi Vert had "personal issues".<ref>{{Citation|last=Power 106 Los Angeles|title=Rich The Kid – Knowledge From Kendrick Lamar, Lil Wayne Convo. Details, And More!|date=February 9, 2018|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9dTGSBPUh18| archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211118/9dTGSBPUh18| archive-date=2021-11-18 | url-status=live|access-date=June 16, 2018}}{{cbignore}}</ref> On February 27, 2018, Rich the Kid previewed a diss track directed at Lil Uzi Vert titled "Dead Friends" with production from DJ Mustard.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/116940-rich-the-kid-fires-shots-at-lil-uzi-vert-on-new-song-preview-news|title=Rich The Kid Fires Shots At Lil Uzi Vert On New Song Preview|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref>

On March 26, 2018, Rich the Kid officially released "Dead Friends" as a single.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/rich-the-kid-dead-friends-new-song-listen-8261443/|title=Rich the Kid Takes Aim at Lil Uzi Vert on 'Dead Friends': Listen|magazine=Billboard|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/04/rich-the-kid-hints-dead-friends-video-is-about-lil-uzi-vert/|title=Rich The Kid Hints "Dead Friends" Video Is About Lil Uzi Vert – XXL|website=XXL Mag|date=April 24, 2018 |access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> Following the release of "Dead Friends", Rich the Kid said he thought Lil Uzi Vert would not respond.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2018/03/rich-the-kid-doesnt-think-lil-uzi-vert-will-respond-to-dead-friends|title=Rich the Kid Doesn't Think Lil Uzi Vert Will Respond to Diss Song "Dead Friends"|website=Complex|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref> Uzi later responded on their SoundCloud with "Rich Forever Leaked" over the [[Chief Keef]] "Where" instrumental, to which Rich the Kid responded by saying "Fuck that nigga."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2018/04/rich-the-kid-has-more-to-say-about-lil-uzi-vert|title=Rich the Kid Responds to Lil Uzi Vert Diss: 'F**k That N***a'|website=Complex|access-date=June 16, 2018}}</ref>
On June 2, 2018, Rich the Kid and Lil Uzi Vert confronted each other at a [[Starbucks]] in Philadelphia. The former ran from the latter shortly after. Videos of the altercation were posted online on social media.<ref>{{cite news |title=Lil Uzi Vert Runs Up On Rich The Kid To Settle Their Beef |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/105969-lil-uzi-vert-runs-up-on-rich-the-kid-to-settle-their-beef-news |access-date=January 7, 2019 |author=Matthew Parizot|work=HotNewHipHop|date=June 3, 2018}}</ref>

