In March 2016, Rich the Kid started his own record label called Rich Forever Music.<ref name="RFM1">{{cite web|url=http://hiphopdx.com/news/id.37793/title.rich-the-kid-launches-rich-forever-music-label-unveils-first-signee|title=Rich The Kid Launches Rich Forever Music; Unveils First Signee|author=Mansell, Henry|date=March 7, 2016|work=[[HipHopDX]]|access-date=August 17, 2016|archive-date=August 18, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818110357/http://hiphopdx.com/news/id.37793/title.rich-the-kid-launches-rich-forever-music-label-unveils-first-signee|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="RFM2">{{cite news|url=http://www.vibe.com/2016/04/rich-the-kid-rich-forever-mixtape/|title=Rich The Kid Introduces His Label With 'Rich Forever Music' Mixtape|author=Robertson, Darryl|date=April 5, 2016|work=[[Vibe (magazine)|Vibe Magazine]]|access-date=August 17, 2016}}</ref> The label's first artist signed up was Chicago based [[Famous Dex]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2016/03/rich-the-kid-signs-famous-dex/|title=Rich The Kid Signs Famous Dex to His New Label|work=[[XXL (magazine)|XXL Magazine]]|last=Ivey|first=Justin|date=March 8, 2016|access-date=July 20, 2016}}</ref> He also signed his first producer to Rich Forever Music, The Lab Cook.<ref name="firstrelease">{{cite web|url=http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-rich-forever-music-new-mixtape.116351.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160406211100/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/rich-the-kid-rich-forever-music-new-mixtape.116351.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=April 6, 2016|title=Rich The Kid – Rich Forever Music|author=Smith, Trevor|date=April 4, 2016|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=August 17, 2016}}</ref> In April 2016, Rich the Kid signed his second artist, rapper J $tash.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.thefader.com/2016/04/04/rich-the-kid-shares-compilation-mixtape-irich-forever-musici|title=Rich The Kid Shares Compilation Mixtape Rich Forever Music|last=Dandridge-Lemco|first=Ben|date=April 4, 2016|work=The Fader|access-date=September 9, 2018}}</ref>

The record label's first release was a 15-track compilation titled ''Rich Forever Music'', and featured [[Offset (rapper)|Offset]], Skippa Da Flippa, [[Lil Yachty]] and [[OG Maco]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.rapswag.com/2016/04/04/mixtape-rich-forever-music/#more-71498|title=Mixtape: Rich Forever Music – Rap Swagger|date=April 4, 2016|work=Rap Swagger|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref> Shortly after the release, J $tash parted ways with the label.

In June 2016, Rich the Kid signed a deal to have [[300 Entertainment]] become a parent company for Rich Forever Music.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://thesource.com/2016/07/05/rich-the-kid-delivers-rich-forever-2-mixtape/|title=Rich The Kid Delivers 'Rich Forever 2' Mixtape|author=Lee, Craig|date=July 5, 2016|work=[[The Source (magazine)|The Source]]}}</ref>

On July 4, 2016, Rich Forever Music released their second project ''Rich Forever 2,'' a collaborative mixtape between Rich the Kid and Famous Dex, with appearances from [[Wiz Khalifa]], Lil Yachty, [[Young Thug]], [[Jaden Smith]] and [[Playboi Carti]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/43616-rich-the-kid-rich-forever-2-new-mixtape|title=Rich Forever 2|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref> In November 2016, Rich the Kid signed [[Brooklyn]] rapper Jay Critch to his label.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2016/12/rich-the-kid-and-jay-critch-got-a-hit-with-did-it-again-remix/|title=Rich The Kid and Jay Critch Got a Hit With "Did It Again (Remix)"|author=C.M Emmanuel|date=December 1, 2016|work=[[XXL Magazine]]}}</ref>

On March 17, 2017, the label released their third compilation mixtape ''The Rich Forever Way''.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/54669-rich-the-kid-the-rich-forever-way-stream-new-mixtape|title=The Rich Forever Way [Stream]|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref> The label released their fourth compilation ''[[Rich Forever 3]]'' on June 16, 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/61471-rich-the-kid-reveals-tracklist-for-rich-forever-3-news|title=Rich The Kid Reveals Tracklist For 'Rich Forever 3'|last=Goddard|first=Kevin|date=June 2, 2017|publisher=Hotnewhiphop.com|access-date=June 6, 2017}}</ref>

In March 2017, he signed [[North Carolina]] rap trio 83 Babies to his label. He appeared on the remix to their song "No Cap".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Thomas |first=Datwon |date=2019-05-18 |title=Rich The Kid Introduces His New Group, 83 Babies With "No Cap" Video |url=https://www.vibe.com/news/entertainment/rich-the-kid-introduces-his-new-group-83-babies-with-no-cap-video-648655/ |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=VIBE.com |language=en-US}}</ref> In October 2017, Lil Tony—one of the group's members—was arrested for murdering a nine-year-old child. In an interview with [[DJ Vlad]], Rich the Kid stated that the group would continue to release music.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Findlay |first=Mitch |date=2020-03-19 |title=Rich The Kid Addresses 83 Babies Rapper's Murder Charge |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/290188-rich-the-kid-addresses-83-babies-rappers-murder-charge-news |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=HotNewHipHop |language=en}}</ref> On July 7, 2022, Lil Tony was sentenced to life in prison.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-10-05 |title=Middle District of North Carolina {{!}} Two Durham Gang Members Sentenced to Life in Prison for the Murder of Nine-Year-Old Z'yon Person {{!}} United States Department of Justice |url=https://www.justice.gov/usao-mdnc/pr/two-durham-gang-members-sentenced-life-prison-murder-nine-year-old-z-yon-person |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=www.justice.gov |language=en}}</ref>

In February 2018, Rich the Kid signed [[Texas]] rapper [[Almighty Jay]] to his label.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.elevatormag.com/ybn-almighty-jay-signs-to-to-rich-forever-ent/|title=YBN Almighty Jay signs to Rich Forever Ent.|date=January 16, 2018|work=Elevator Mag|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref> In March 2018, YBN Almighty Jay and Rich the Kid had a fall out when Rich the Kid released a song called ''Back Quick'' without YBN Almighty Jay's permission.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/119013-ybn-almighty-jay-attempts-to-pull-up-on-rich-the-kid-in-possibly-fake-beef-news|title=YBN Almighty Jay Attempts To "Pull Up" On Rich The Kid In Possibly Fake Beef|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=September 26, 2018}}</ref> In April 2018, YBN Almighty Jay did an interview with [[DJ Akademiks]] saying he was never signed with the label.<ref>{{cite web|publisher=[[YouTube]]|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wLyq4gS0sjM| archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211118/wLyq4gS0sjM| archive-date=2021-11-18 | url-status=live|title=YBN Almighty Jay Says he was NEVER Signed to Rich Forever & Tells why He almost Fought Rich the Kid!|author=DJ Akademiks|date=April 18, 2018|access-date=September 26, 2018}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fNBTODG2cNE| archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211118/fNBTODG2cNE| archive-date=2021-11-18 | url-status=live|title=YBN Almighty Jay Says He never signed to Rich the Kid and speaks on YBN Nahmir vs Lil Wop!|website=YouTube|author=King Akademiks|date=April 18, 2018|access-date=September 26, 2018}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

In May 2018, Famous Dex stated he had left Rich Forever Music, and is an independent artist,<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/150775-famous-dex-announces-his-departure-from-rich-the-kids-rich-forever-label-news|title=Famous Dex Announces His Departure From Rich The Kid's "Rich Forever" Label|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=May 31, 2018}}</ref> but shortly after, Rich the Kid stated through the label's Instagram page that he is still signed with the label.<ref>[https://bibliogram.pussthecat.org/p/BjaHxmDleAH Non-loginwalled link at bibliogram.pussthecat.org]: {{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BjaHxmDleAH/|title=Rich Forever Music on Instagram: "Like it or not he is Rich Forever @famousdex ✍🏽🤦🏾♂️"|website=Instagram|access-date=November 18, 2018}}</ref>

