'''Jacob Anthony Perez''' (born April 21, 1996), better known as '''Princeton Perez''', is an American singer-songwriter, professional dancer, and actor. Born and raised in [[Downey, California]], near Los Angeles, Perez began his career at a young age when he appeared in television advertisements for companies such as [[Nike, Inc.|Nike]], [[McDonald's]], and [[Skechers]]. Perez later rose to fame as a member of the boy band [[Mindless Behavior]], in which he remained from 2008 until the group's disbandment in 2017.

==Life and career==
===2006–2008: Early life and career beginnings===
Perez was born in [[Downey, California]] to an African-American father and Mexican mother. In 2006, Perez was cast in two Gym Class Heroes music videos. "[[Shoot Down the Stars]]" followed him as a younger version of [[Travie McCoy]], being bullied by other students. "[[Cupid's Chokehold]]", however portrayed him as a young [[Cupid]], shooting Travie with a bow and arrow, causing the rapper to express his love for various women in the video.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eiiU-Fky18s|title=Gym Class Heroes: Cupid's Chokehold ft. Patrick Stump [OFFICIAL VIDEO]|date=November 28, 2006 |via=YouTube|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=swIOB-YTWQM Princeton as Cupid Boy]. YouTube (October 7, 2013). Retrieved 1 March 2017.</ref> In an interview with [[AwesomenessTV]], Perez has stated that he had also danced backup for [[Nicole Scherzinger]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qkINVGHdLvg|title=Mindless Takeover – Mindless Behavior Meet Nicole Scherzinger – Mindless Takeover Ep. 2|date=June 23, 2012 |via=YouTube|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref>

At the age of 11, Perez appeared on commercials for [[Skechers]], [[McDonald's]] and [[Nike, Inc.|Nike]], which helped progress his career in entertainment. He was also cast in ''[[High School Musical 3]]'', playing a small part as the young [[Corbin Bleu]], but he could not take the role as it was around the same time he became a member of Mindless Behavior. Perez had worked with choreographers such as [[Dave Scott (choreographer)|Dave Scott]] and Kaelynn Harris of [[8 Flavahz]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bet.com/photo-gallery/oujkfk/10-things-you-didn-t-know-about-mindless-behavior/hd9wwe|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251017122402/https://www.bet.com/photo-gallery/oujkfk/10-things-you-didn-t-know-about-mindless-behavior/hd9wwe|url-status=dead|archive-date=October 17, 2025|title=10 Things You Didn't Know About Mindless Behavior|date=February 7, 2013|work=BET.com|access-date=October 14, 2014}}</ref>

===2008–14: Mindless Behavior: ''#1 Girl'' and ''All Around the World''===
Lakeisha Gamble, one of the contributing founders of Mindless Behavior, convinced future producer of the group, Walter Millsap, to form an American boy band.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://plus.google.com/+MindlessBehavior/posts/X285zMtMtBv|title=#TEAMMINDLESS: MB started with Keisha & Walter|work=Google Plus|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.kidzworld.com/article/24613-mindless-behavior-qanda|title=Mindless Behavior Q&A|work=Kidzworld.com|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref> He was opposed to the idea at first, as explained in the film, ''[[Mindless Behavior: All Around the World]]''.<ref name="autogenerated1">{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/artists/mindless-behavior/biography/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130206020522/http://www.mtv.com/artists/mindless-behavior/biography/|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 6, 2013|title=About Mindless Behavior|publisher=MTV|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2012/music/news/mindless-behavior-r-b-band-conquers-youtube-takes-aim-at-top-40-1118058847/|title=Mindless Behavior: R&B band conquers YouTube, takes aim at Top 40|work=Variety|date=September 14, 2012 |accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref> Dave Scott, a choreographer with prior experience working with Perez at the Debbie Allen Academy, had been recommended to contact Perez to audition for the group after seeing him in Gym Class Heroes' music videos.<ref name="autogenerated1"/><ref name="youtube1">{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZePYg4dtJN0&feature=youtube&t=32|title=Mindless Behavior: London Live 2013 HD|via=YouTube|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref><ref name="gazettereview1">{{cite web|url=http://gazettereview.com/2015/11/what-happened-to-mindless-behavior-the-latest-updates-news/|title=What happened to Mindless Behavior – The Latest Updates & News for 2017|work=Gazette Review|accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref> Perez received approval to join the new group within the same night and had been the first member to be selected, preceding [[Santo August|Chresanto "Roc Royal" August]], Rayan "Ray Ray" Lopez, and Craig "Prodigy" Crippen.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mindlessbehavior.com/record-label/interscope|title=Interscope|work=mindlessbehavior.com|accessdate=October 14, 2014|url-status=dead|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20141006185836/http://www.mindlessbehavior.com/record-label/interscope|archivedate=October 6, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.linkedin.com/pub/mindless-behavior/54/70a/142|title=Mindless Behavior|publisher=Linkedin.com|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mindlessbehavior.com/bio.html|title=#aboutMB|work=mindlessbehavior.com|accessdate=October 12, 2013}}{{Dead link|date=July 2024 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> Gamble, inspired by [[Princeton University]], had given Perez the alias, owing to his extensive knowledge of diverse music genres.<ref name="youtube1"/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LPEVs0FV7Os|title=Mindless Behavior: All Around the World (1/11) Movie CLIP – Princeton (2013) HD|via=YouTube|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref>

For two years, the group immersed themselves in music, developing their musical sound and style under the guidance of Herbert and Millsap.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.popdust.com/mindless-behavior-lol-ing-all-the-way-to-stardom-1889153833.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224212140/http://www.popdust.com/mindless-behavior-lol-ing-all-the-way-to-stardom-1889153833.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 24, 2017|title=Mindless Behavior: LOL-ing All The Way To Stardom|work=popdust.com|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.janetjackson.com/news/topic/janet-jackson-launches-teen-group-mindless-behavior-on-her-us-tour#.WK-niDsrK00|title=JANET JACKSON LAUNCHES TEEN GROUP MINDLESS BEHAVIOR, ON HER U.S. TOUR|work=Janetjackson.com|accessdate=February 23, 2017|archive-date=February 24, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224133610/http://www.janetjackson.com/news/topic/janet-jackson-launches-teen-group-mindless-behavior-on-her-us-tour#.WK-niDsrK00|url-status=dead}}</ref> Building their performance repertoire, they staged shows at local schools as part of the CLASSCFIED High School Tour and engaged with their growing fanbase through creative content such as their "MB Cam" [[YouTube]] [[vlog]] channel.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/goingoutguide/mindless-behavior-all-around-the-world-movie-review/2013/03/15/daeae1f6-8db8-11e2-9f54-f3fdd70acad2_story.html|title='Mindless Behavior: All Around the World' movie review|newspaper=The Washington Post|accessdate=February 23, 2017}}</ref> Following these efforts, [[Interscope Records]] chairman [[Jimmy Iovine]] signed Mindless Behavior to the label.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/455162-youth-wave-hnhh-talks-to-mindless-behavior-and-jacob-latimore-news|title=Youth Wave: HNHH Talks To Mindless Behavior And Jacob Latimore|work=Hotnewhiphop.com|date=August 6, 2012 |access-date=February 23, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/mindless-behavior-21-under-21-2013-5727196/|title=18. Mindless Behavior: 21 Under 21 (2013)|magazine=Billboard|access-date=February 23, 2017}}</ref> Mindless Behavior toured with [[The Backstreet Boys]], [[Jason Derulo]], [[Justin Bieber]], and was an opening act for [[Janet Jackson]] during her [[Number Ones, Up Close and Personal]] tour.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1656967/mindless-behavior-justin-bieber-tour/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140903191556/http://www.mtv.com/news/1656967/mindless-behavior-justin-bieber-tour/|url-status=dead|archive-date=September 3, 2014|title=Mindless Behavior Say Touring With Justin Bieber Was 'Crazy'|publisher=MTV News|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1661847/janet-jackson-mindless-behavior/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140903191551/http://www.mtv.com/news/1661847/janet-jackson-mindless-behavior/|url-status=dead|archive-date=September 3, 2014|title=Mindless Behavior Call Meeting Janet Jackson 'Heaven'|publisher=MTV News|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref> The group had grown in popularity from frequently appearing on BET's [[106 & Park]], and also headlined the first BET Closer to My Dreams Tour alongside [[Diggy Simmons]], [[Lil Twist]], Trevante and Jawan Harris. In 2011, Mindless Behavior headlined the [[Scream Tour]] with Diggy Simmons, which featured [[The OMG Girlz]], [[Jacob Latimore]], and Hamilton Park.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://hiphopwired.com/2011/08/19/diggy-simmons-mindless-behavior-hamilton-park-headlining-the-2011-scream-tour/|title=Diggy Simmons, Mindless Behavior, Hamilton Park Headlining The 2011 Scream Tour|work=Hip-Hop Wired|date=August 19, 2011 |accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref> The group performed at the [[White House]] three times, and were the first African-American boy band to do so.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://clizbeats.com/mindless-behavior-to-attend-easter-egg-roll-at-the-white-house4201103/|title=Mindless Behavior To Attend Easter Egg Roll at the White House|work=Clizbeats|date=April 20, 2011 |accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nbcwashington.com/news/local/celebrities-in-dc-for-inauguration-187546501.html|title=Celebrities Hit D.C. for Inauguration|work=NBC Washington|date=January 19, 2013 |accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bckonline.com/2013/01/21/mindless-behavior-perform-at-kids-inaugural-ball/|title=MINDLESS BEHAVIOR PERFORM AT KIDS INAUGURAL BALL|work=BCK Online|date=January 21, 2013 |accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref> They were notable performers at [[Arthur Ashe Kids' Day]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.arthurashekidsday.com/videos/2012-arthur-ashe-kids-day-mindless-behavior/|title=2012 Arthur Ashe Kids' Day: Mindless Behavior|work=arthurashekidsday.com|accessdate=February 21, 2017|archive-date=February 22, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170222111130/http://www.arthurashekidsday.com/videos/2012-arthur-ashe-kids-day-mindless-behavior/|url-status=dead}}</ref>

In 2012, Mindless Behavior embarked on their headlined U.S. tour, named after their debut album "No. 1 Girl," with opening acts Jacob Latimore, Lil Twist, and Kayla Brianna.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.richmondcenterstage.com/news/mindless-behavior-announces-us-1-girl-tour-kick-richmond-carpenter-theatre-richmond-centerstage|title=MINDLESS BEHAVIOR ANNOUNCES U.S. "#1 GIRL TOUR" TO KICK OFF IN RICHMOND AT CARPENTER THEATRE AT RICHMOND CENTERSTAGE THURSDAY, JULY 5, 2012 AT 7&nbsp;pm|publisher=Richmondcenterstage.com|accessdate=October 14, 2014|archive-date=September 3, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140903062413/http://www.richmondcenterstage.com/news/mindless-behavior-announces-us-1-girl-tour-kick-richmond-carpenter-theatre-richmond-centerstage|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.richmondcenterstage.com/event/mindless-behavior-1-girl-tour-special-guest-jacob-latimore|title=Mindless Behavior No. 1 Girl Tour with special guest Jacob Latimore – Richmond CenterStage|publisher=Richmondcenterstage.com|accessdate=October 14, 2014|archive-date=June 23, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120623023240/http://richmondcenterstage.com/event/mindless-behavior-1-girl-tour-special-guest-jacob-latimore|url-status=dead}}</ref> While on tour, the group visited the [[Ronald McDonald House]] in Georgia to be of comfort for the young patients who were battling cancer.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://crossroadsnews.com/news/2012/aug/16/mindless-behavior-meets-sick-kids-at-ronald/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170222195842/http://crossroadsnews.com/news/2012/aug/16/mindless-behavior-meets-sick-kids-at-ronald/|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 22, 2017|title=Mindless Behavior meets sick kids at Ronald McDonald House|publisher=Crossroadnews.com|accessdate=February 21, 2017}}</ref> In 2013, the group performed for Wade's World Foundation, an organization by [[Dwyane Wade]] that provides support to community-based organizations that promote education, health and social skills for children in at-risk situations.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.dnainfo.com/chicago/20130904/downtown/dwyane-wades-charitable-foundation-celebrates-10th-anniversary|title=Dwyane Wade's Charitable Foundation Celebrates 10th Anniversary|work=DNAINFO|accessdate=February 21, 2017|url-status=dead|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170222112510/https://www.dnainfo.com/chicago/20130904/downtown/dwyane-wades-charitable-foundation-celebrates-10th-anniversary|archivedate=February 22, 2017}}</ref> Following the release of their sophomore album "All Around The World", the group embarked on their eponymous tour, featuring The OMG Girlz and Coco Jones.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rap-up.com/2013/05/13/mindless-behavior-announces-all-around-the-world-tour/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131024134732/http://www.rap-up.com/2013/05/13/mindless-behavior-announces-all-around-the-world-tour/|url-status=dead|archive-date=October 24, 2013|title=MINDLESS BEHAVIOR ANNOUNCES 'ALL AROUND THE WORLD' TOUR|work=Rap-up.com|accessdate=February 24, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.aeglive.com/news/view/12057|title=Mindless Behavior's "All Around The World Tour" Featuring The OMG Girlz, Coco Jones and Young Marqus, is All Around Social Media|work=Aeglive.com|accessdate=February 24, 2017}}</ref> Subsequent to the tour, news sources began speculating about the addition of a new member to the group following the departure of lead singer Prodigy. For nearly two years, Mindless Behavior continued to perform, albeit without a lead vocalist. Elijah Johnson replaced him as the lead singer in April 2014.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rap-up.com/2014/04/04/mindless-behavior-announces-new-member/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150203044235/http://www.rap-up.com/2014/04/04/mindless-behavior-announces-new-member/|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 3, 2015|title=RapUp.com – Mindless Behavior Announces New Member|work=Rap-Up.com|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref> Mindless Behavior later signed a deal with [[Epic Records]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://thatgrapejuice.net/2014/07/mindless-behavior-sign-epic-records/|title=Mindless Behavior Sign With Epic Records|work=..::That Grape Juice // ThatGrapeJuice.net::.. – Thirsty?|date=July 10, 2014 |accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref>

===2015–16: Group changes and ''#OfficialMBMusic''===
[[File:Princeton's 20th birthday photoshoot.jpg|thumb|250x250px|Perez in 2016, attending a photoshoot for his 20th birthday|left]]
During the hiatus of Mindless Behavior, Perez actively engaged with Team Mindless, their dedicated fanbase, by regularly sharing photos, videos, and short films on his blog, Outsiders Ink.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://iammekhi.weebly.com/turnertvinc/mindless-behaviors-princeton-releases-new-photos-from-personal-blog|title=Mindless behavior's: princeton releases new photos from personal blog|work=Iammekhi Blog|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://vimeo.com/104387530|title=Ooutsider's Ink|work=ZAEBEARPHOTO|access-date=October 14, 2014}}</ref> In an interview that featured the group in January 2015, both Perez and Lopez ("Ray Ray") stated they had been working on their own solo projects outside of the group.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TVmxMa1xRKE|title=Block DVD Mindless Behavior Interview|date=January 8, 2015 |via=YouTube|access-date=January 15, 2017}}</ref> Perez independently released "Don't Believe in Love" via SoundCloud, a track blending reggae fusion and pop influences, amassing over 800,000 listens before later being removed from Perez's account.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://soundcloud.com/mr-pottymouth/dont-believe-in-love|title=Don't Believe in Love|work=SoundCloud|access-date=January 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SjDpjvA725k|title=Don't Believe In Love by Mr. Pottymouth (Princeton) (Lyrics)|work=YouTube|date=January 11, 2015 |access-date=April 27, 2024}}</ref> Subsequent to the departure of August ("Roc Royal") from Mindless Behavior, management replaced him with vocalist Michael "Mike River" Martin, and the group embarked on the creation of their third studio album, which was ultimately shelved.<ref name="gazettereview1"/><ref>{{cite web|url=http://music.allaccess.com/an-interview-with-mindless-behavior-about-their-soon-to-be-released-album/|title=An Interview With MINDLESS BEHAVIOR About Their Soon-To-Be Released Album!|work=All Access|date=June 28, 2016|access-date=January 15, 2017|archive-date=December 30, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161230231213/http://music.allaccess.com/an-interview-with-mindless-behavior-about-their-soon-to-be-released-album/|url-status=dead}}</ref> Following this, Lopez also exited the group, citing creative differences, leaving Perez as the sole remaining original member from the band's inception in 2008.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ki4BJL4a4vE|title=Rayan 'Why I Left Mindless Behavior'|date=February 7, 2016 |via=YouTube|accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref>

With the abandonment of the project, the group redirected their efforts, later releasing the group's final album, #OfficialMBMusic, in 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bet.com/article/qducv1/premiere-mindless-behavior-drops-new-album|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241228142618/https://www.bet.com/article/qducv1/premiere-mindless-behavior-drops-new-album|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 28, 2024|title=Premiere: Mindless Behavior Drops New Album '#OFFICIALMBMUSIC' Ahead of BET Experience|work=BET|access-date=January 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://singersroom.com/content/2016-04-08/mindless-behavior-returns-with-two-new-members-a-new-single-song-cry/|title=Mindless Behavior Returns With Two New Members & A New Single, 'Song Cry'|work=BET|access-date=January 15, 2017}}</ref> After the album release, the group began shooting ''[[Misguided Behavior]]'', a drama film directed by [[Carl Payne]], starring Clifton Powell, Towanda Braxton, and Khalil Kain.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://thegrio.com/2018/11/20/exclusive-misguided-behavior-shows-sinister-consequences-bullying-and-encourages-parents-to-spot-the-signs/|title=EXCLUSIVE: 'Misguided Behavior' shows sinister consequences of bullying and encourages parents to spot the signs|work=The Grio|date=November 20, 2018 |access-date=April 27, 2024}}</ref> Concurrently, Mindless Behavior unveiled their "#NoParentsAllowed" tour in September 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://raycornelius.com/2016/09/mindless-behavior-announce-no-parents-allowed-tour/|title=MINDLESS BEHAVIOR ANNOUNCE 'NO PARENTS ALLOWED' TOUR|work=Ray Cornelius|accessdate=February 4, 2017}}</ref> Sponsored by Alcatel in support of their latest studio album, the 23-city tour was initially set to kick off on November 9 in Greensboro, North Carolina; however, in November 2016, all group members announced the postponement of the tour, with various ticket websites reflecting its cancellation.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.timeout.com/detroit/things-to-do/cancelled-mindless-behavior-no-parents-allowed-tour|title=Cancelled Mindless Behavior No Parents Allowed Tour|work=Time Out|date=December 10, 2016 |access-date=February 4, 2017}}</ref> In a [[YouNow]], Perez communicated with fans, explaining that the group does not control tour dates, and had been trying to schedule dates since earlier that year.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://youtube.com/ix9-NepRJTU?t=139|title=Princeton's YouNow (9/22/16)|via=YouTube|access-date=February 4, 2017}}{{dead link|date=November 2017 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

===2017–present: Solo career and ''Papi Chulo Prelude''===
In 2017, Perez addressed a fan on Instagram about the group's hiatus, suggesting that the music industry's structure hindered their creative freedom and hinting that if "certain managers" and record labels granted Mindless Behavior ownership of their music and group name, they could produce more music; prior to this, widespread rumors of the band disbanding were dispelled by bandmate Mike River.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BP6Bk_og9w9/|title=Honey|work=Instagram|accessdate=February 4, 2017}}</ref> In February, Perez took to Twitter to publicly declare Mindless Behavior's disbandment, citing the group's inability to secure rights to their music and their desire to pursue individual endeavors.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/theoneprinceton/status/833149183792066560|title=well I'm not lol but still be an artist or a writer or something|work=Twitter|accessdate=February 19, 2017}}</ref> On February 23, the tracklist for [[Taylor Bennett (rapper)|Taylor Bennett's]] project, "Restoration of An American Idol," was unveiled, with Perez featured in the introductory track titled "The Kid's Alright."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/02/taylor-bennetts-restoration-of-an-american-idol-features-chance-the-rapper-lil-yachty/|title=Taylor Bennett's New Project 'Restoration of an American Idol' Features Chance The Rapper, Lil Yachty and More|work=xxlmag.com|date=February 23, 2017 |accessdate=February 24, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/470560-chance-the-rapper-lil-yachty-and-more-feature-on-taylor-bennetts-new-project-news|title=Chance The Rapper, Lil Yachty & More Feature on Taylor Bennett's New Project|work=hotnewhiphop.com|date=February 23, 2017 |access-date=February 24, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/theoneprinceton/status/833152313640439809|title=we just grew up and wanted to do individual stuff, lol can't be in a group forever!|work=Twitter|accessdate=February 19, 2017}}</ref>{{Primary source inline|date=July 2018}} In March, Perez appeared on the cover of 360 Magazine, marking his inaugural solo magazine cover following the disbandment of Mindless Behavior.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://360magazineblog.wordpress.com/2017/04/06/love-peace-x-princeton/|title=LOVE, PEACE × PRINCETON PEREZ|work=360 Magazine|date=April 6, 2017 |accessdate=April 6, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/360Magazine/status/849034392810815488|title=TODAY at 4:30&nbsp;pm PST / 7:30&nbsp;pm EST @theoneprinceton will conduct a '360 LIVE Instagram Vid Chat' on our account⤵|work=Twitter|accessdate=April 6, 2017}}</ref> In April, on the eve of his twenty-first birthday, Perez appeared the cover of Obvious Magazine, followed by a feature on the cover of Tinsley Magazine in June.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BTKKFBTATFz/|title=Behind-the-scenes with @theoneprinceton. His cover shoot ended up being like a birthday gift (his birthday is today). |work=Instagram|accessdate=April 21, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/mefeater/status/870789248663814144|title=Princeton Perez for Tinsley Magazine|work=Twitter|accessdate=January 24, 2018}}</ref>

That year, Perez was invited as a guest to the Las Vegas Teen Town Hall, where he joined former Mindless Behavior group member [[Elijah Johnson (singer)|Elijah Johnson]] and [[Diamond White]]. Hosted by City Councilman Ricki Y. Barlow, the event was attended by representatives from ten different high schools within the district. As part of the event, Barlow presented a proclamation from the city of Las Vegas, officially declaring May 30 as Diamond White, Elijah "EJ" Johnson, and Jacob "Princeton" Perez Day, recognizing and honoring the contributions of each guest.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://area-info.net/councilman-ricki-y-barlow-to-host-teen-town-hall/|title=Councilman Ricki Y. Barlow To Host Teen Town Hall|work=area-info.net|accessdate=May 31, 2017|archive-date=July 15, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180715093608/https://area-info.net/councilman-ricki-y-barlow-to-host-teen-town-hall/|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ktnv.com/positivelylv/education/students-attend-teen-town-hall-in-las-vegas|title=Students attend Teen Town Hall in Las Vegas|work=ktnv.com|date=May 31, 2017 |accessdate=May 31, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/theoneprinceton/status/869690067190661120|title=May 30th is now officially 'Princeton Perez Day' in Las Vegas!|work=Twitter|accessdate=May 31, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://youtube.com/txqWy-VbDns?t=3432|title=Teen Town Hall 2017|work=KCLV-TV Las Vegas City of Las Vegas Television|accessdate=May 31, 2017}}{{Dead link|date=November 2018 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> At the [[BET Experience]] preceding the [[BET Awards 2017]], Perez served as the host for the [[Teen Summit]] panel, a program that had been absent from syndication since 2002.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bet.com/bet-experience/2017/content/Articles/teen-summit-returns-for-the-culture.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170625231929/http://www.bet.com/bet-experience/2017/content/Articles/teen-summit-returns-for-the-culture.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=June 25, 2017|title=Teen Summit Returns for the Culture
|work=BET|accessdate=June 27, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BVxjCOUlpFn/|title=Come through to my #teensummit panel to talk about the influence of music and social media today at #betx! Panel starts at 3&nbsp;pm PST! I'll be hosting|work=Instagram|accessdate=June 27, 2017}}</ref> Furthermore, in collaboration with Obvious Magazine, Perez a tour spanning several cities across the United States; however, the tour was ultimately cancelled due to scheduling conflicts arising from Perez's commitment to filming #WarGames.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://obviousmag.com/Princeton-Perez/|title=PRINCETON X OBVIOUS POP-UP|work=Obvious Magazine|accessdate=June 27, 2017}}{{Dead link|date=February 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> In 2018, Perez had been gearing up for the release of his debut solo music record, produced by Timeless Music Group; subsequently, on June 12, 2019, "Perfect World" made its debut on the Tidal music streaming service.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.flaunt.com/blog/princeton-perez|title="PERFECT WORLD" - PRINCETON PEREZ MAKES RECORDS FOR CONCERTS|work=Flaunt Magazine|accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.timelessmusicgroupllc.com/single-post/2017/12/25/TMG-is-having-the-please-of-executively-producing-Princeton-Perez-Solo-release-This-is-his-first-solo-release-since-his-group-Mindless-behavior|title=TMG is having the pleasure of executively producing Princeton Perez Solo release!|work=Timeless Music Group|accessdate=January 23, 2018|archive-date=January 24, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180124070933/http://www.timelessmusicgroupllc.com/single-post/2017/12/25/TMG-is-having-the-please-of-executively-producing-Princeton-Perez-Solo-release-This-is-his-first-solo-release-since-his-group-Mindless-behavior|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/princetonperez/status/1136047326496141312|title=after Mindless Behavior decided to split & do our own individual stuff, I decided to take my time & start recording my solo E.P & get back into artist development! I know I've been posting some song snippets & been saying "coming soon" buuut, I cant hold back anymore!! soo...|work=Twitter|accessdate=June 13, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yxFMpZQYGx4|title=Princeton Ready To Launch SOLO Career (Song Snippets)|work=YouTube|accessdate=June 13, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://tidal.com/browse/track/109927573|title=Perfect World by Princeton Perez|work=Tidal|accessdate=June 13, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://read.tidal.com/article/princeton-perez-perfect-world|title=PRINCETON PEREZ DROPS A NEW TRACK — AND A LETTER TO HIS YOUNGER SELF|work=Tidal|date=June 12, 2019 |accessdate=June 13, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://genius.com/Princeton-perez-perfect-world-lyrics|title=Princeton Perez, Perfect World|work=Genius|accessdate=June 13, 2019}}</ref> In August, Perez was a guest on [[Angela Yee]]'s Lip Service Podcast.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=utUsctffDkI|title=Angela Yee's Lip Service Ft. Sarunas Jackson & Princeton Perez
|work=YouTube|accessdate=March 2, 2019}}</ref> In December 2019, Perez released the Christmas in Malibu EP.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://parlemag.com/entertainment-news/princeton-perez-christmas/|title=Princeton Perez Brings in the Holiday Season with New Christmas EP|work=Parle Mag|date=December 20, 2019 |accessdate=March 2, 2024}}</ref>

{{Quote box|align=left|width=30em|quote="Transitioning from a group to a solo artist, it's been organic because originally I wasn't planning on going solo. I didn't have a plan, but I think that's why it worked out."|source =—Perez, regarding his decision to pursue a solo career.<ref name=":1">{{Cite news |url=https://hollywoodlife.com/2019/12/06/princeton-perez-transition-mindless-behavior-solo-artist-organic/|title=Princeton Perez: Why His Transition From Mindless Behavior To A Solo Artist Was 'Organic'|work=HollywoodLife|access-date=April 27, 2024}}</ref>}}

In 2020, Perez released his single "Chew It Up," which gained substantial traction on the social media platform TikTok, alongside the release of a music video for his single "Control".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://parlemag.com/entertainment-news/princeton-perez-christmas/|title=Princeton Perez - Control (Official Video)|work=YouTube|date=December 20, 2019 |accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://thisisrnb.com/2020/02/princeton-perez-releases-video-for-control/|title=PRINCETON PEREZ RELEASES VIDEO FOR "CONTROL"|work=ThisIsRNB|date=February 4, 2020 |accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref> In August 2023, Perez made an appearance in the music video for "Dance To The Rhythm" by Dia La Ren Nash, the daughter of [[Niecy Nash]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-5g2R5a2V8k|title="Dance" To The Rhythm (OFFICIAL MUSIC VIDEO)|work=YouTube|date=August 28, 2023 |accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref> Perez later released the single "Suelo" — clarifying that it would be part of a Spanish-speaking project later to be released.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pOnRYWiPyaI|title=Suelo (Official Audio) - Princeton Perez
|work=YouTube|date=September 24, 2023
|accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref>

==Style and influences==
Perez has stated that his influences, both fashion, musicality, and performance are [[John Lennon]], [[Prince (musician)|Prince]], [[Michael Jackson]], [[David Bowie]], [[Usher (musician)|Usher]], [[Chris Brown]], and a few rock bands, including [[Nirvana (band)|Nirvana]], [[Sublime (band)|Sublime]] and [[The Misfits (band)|The Misfits]], the latter of which inspiring his original [[Instagram]] handle "princemisfit" and later, "peacepunkprince".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://singersroom.com/content/2019-08-16/the-prelude-to-princeton-perez-groomed-for-promise-and-ready-to-take-off-interview/|title=MThe Prelude To Princeton Perez: Groomed For Promise And Ready To Take Off (Interview)|work=SingersRoom|accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.augustachronicle.com/story/entertainment/music/2012/07/25/mindless-behavior-finds-success-through-teen-fans/14489283007/|title=Mindless Behavior finds success through teen fans
|work=Agusta Chronicle|accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.aol.com/mindless-behaviors-princeton-perez-talks-about-his-career-as-a-triple-threat-and-life-after-the-band-171536312.html|title=Mindless Behavior's Princeton Perez talks about his career as a triple threat and life after the band|work=AOL|date=August 26, 2020 |accessdate=April 27, 2024}}</ref> Perez's fascination with fashion was apparent, characterized by his androgynous style, and a unique blend influenced by punk-rock, grunge bands, and a nostalgic nod to 1970s hippie culture.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.kidzworld.com/article/28355-exclusive-mindless-behavior-princeton-gets-personal|title= EXCLUSIVE! Mindless Behavior: Princeton Gets Personal!|work=Kidzworld|accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://radio.com/2013/04/25/princeton-mindless-behavior-rock-t-shirt-collection/|title=Style Files: Princeton Of Mindless Behavior Talks Rock T-Shirt Collection|work=Radio.com|accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.co.uk/the-wrap-up/blog/mindless-behavior-the-interview|title=mindless behavior: the interview!|work=MTV UK|accessdate=October 14, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170224133308/http://www.mtv.co.uk/the-wrap-up/blog/mindless-behavior-the-interview|archive-date=February 24, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> He participated as a judge in the "Face of Spoiled Show & Contest" with [[Eva Marcille]] in July 2014.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.gettyimages.com/detail/news-photo/princeton-attends-face-of-spoiled-annual-fashion-show-news-photo/452770368|title=Princeton attends Face of Spoiled Annual Fashion Show Contest|work=Getty Images|date=July 27, 2014 |accessdate=October 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://spoiledfashionz.com/pages/face-of-spoiled-2014-finale|title=FACE of SPOILED! 2014 Finale..HOSTED by EVA MARCILLE and PRINCETON|work=Spoiled Fashionz|accessdate=January 15, 2017|url-status=dead|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170202150210/https://spoiledfashionz.com/pages/face-of-spoiled-2014-finale|archivedate=February 2, 2017}}</ref>

==Advocacy==
Princeton has openly supported [[People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals]] and its initiatives to end the mistreatment and abuse of animals.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.peta2.com/blog/celebs-freedom/|title=Celebs Fighting for Freedom for All|work=Peta2|accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref> In a 2015 campaign for the peta2's Hottest Vegetarian Celebrities, Princeton won alongside [[Zendaya]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.peta2.com/heroes/hottest-vegetarian-celebrities-contest-2015/|title=WINNERS: 2015's Hottest Veg Celebs!|work=Peta2|accessdate=January 15, 2017}}</ref>

